.TH sam-jail-update 1 2026-11-23 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail\-update \- Download the newest published version of an app\*(Aqs AppImage and put it in place of the old one (kept, so `\-\-undo` can go back). Settings and files stay
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail update\fR [\fB\-\-undo\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\-key\-change\fR] [\fB\-\-decline\-key\-change\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIAPP\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download the newest published version of an app\*(Aqs AppImage and put it in place of the old one (kept, so `\-\-undo` can go back). Settings and files stay
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-undo\fR
Go back to the version the last update replaced
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\-key\-change\fR
Install the download the last run refused because its signing key changed, its signature could not be checked, or when it was signed could not be read: exactly that file, while it is still the published one (never a new download)
.TP
\fB\-\-decline\-key\-change\fR
Delete the download the last run kept for that answer, without installing it (one never answered is deleted after a week)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIAPP\fR>

